V9-N2 "L2RM+A" (package docs/05 §1, §6: the official L2RM route — OT / partial-OT rematching kept in full — with the SAME trusted anchor budget).
Applies to the official L2RM code (https://github.com/hhc1997/L2RM @ a766c22, file main_L2RM.py; data.py receives the observed mapping exactly as
in ncr_anchor_assisted.diff, since L2RM's PrecompDataset / PrecompDataset_split copy NCR's noise-index logic).  One change in main_L2RM.py: after
the BMM split, anchor pairs are always in the "correct" loader (the anchor-supervised term with weight 1); the rematching of the noisy loader,
the cost network, the queue and the Sym-KL loss are untouched.  The printed "acc" diagnostics use the official clean labels, which the V9
setting does not expose to the trainer: they are skipped when labels are -1.
